WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:12.000
My goodness. GPT-4 barely came out just&nbsp;
a few days ago, and plugin support has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.540
already arrived. What does that mean? It&nbsp;
means supercharging GPT-4 by letting it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:25.620
build on other applications. That is going to&nbsp;
be a game changer. Here are a few incredible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:31.680
examples that showcase the power of this&nbsp;
system so you can also get more out of it.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:39.480
One, meal planning. Now, you may be wondering&nbsp;
why we are using a powerful mathematical system,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:47.160
Wolfram Alpha for a meal, but you’ll see,&nbsp;
just wait a moment. Now we are asking for one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:54.600
restaurant recommendation and a simple recipe for&nbsp;
the next day. And now, watch the magic of plugins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.600 --> 00:01:02.820
happen. ChatGPT recommends us a restaurant, and,&nbsp;
here comes the first plugin - this allows us to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:09.540
just click here and reserve a table. Then, we&nbsp;
get our recipe recommendation, chickpea salad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:16.380
and now comes the magic: Wolfram Alpha&nbsp;
immediately helps us calculate the amount&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:22.560
of calories in the meal. Wow. Finally, if we like&nbsp;
what we are seeing here, with the third plugin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:28.920
ordering the ingredients is just one click away.&nbsp;
Now that is what I call an amazing assistant.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:35.400
And don’t forget, this is a chat assistant, so if&nbsp;
we are looking for something with fewer calories,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:43.080
we can just ask again and it will calculate&nbsp;
and arrange everything for us. I love it.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:48.780
And while we are talking about having&nbsp;
an assistant, check this out. Two. Here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:53.820
we are interested in knowing a little&nbsp;
more about the Oscar winner movies and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:59.100
their box office performance compared&nbsp;
to others. And, hold on to your papers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:06.480
and look at that! It is browsing the internet,&nbsp;
tells us what is searched for, where it clicked,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:13.860
it now knows about the awards, looks up box&nbsp;
office performance, and then, the most important:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:21.720
synthesizes all this information and boils it&nbsp;
down to what we asked for. That is incredible.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:27.480
And it cites its sources too, so if we&nbsp;
are asking about something critical,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:33.600
like the good Fellow Scholars we are, we&nbsp;
can also double-check ourselves. So good!

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:40.500
And if we give it an image, it tells us what&nbsp;
it depicts. That is already quite cool in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:46.380
and of itself, but now comes the assistant&nbsp;
part. Without touching any software tool,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:52.980
and requiring any sort of computer expertise, we&nbsp;
can just write a line and ask it to resize it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.980 --> 00:03:00.720
then, make it grayscale. You know what,&nbsp;
little AI, give it a green tint. Finally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:07.080
we can ask for the foreground only, and&nbsp;
a download link. Now, don’t get me wrong,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:14.160
none of these tasks are difficult to someone who&nbsp;
can code or use some other piece of software to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:20.700
accomplish this. But, you don’t need any of&nbsp;
that now. Just imagine how many millions of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:26.940
people will be able to use the power of today’s&nbsp;
computers without needing to be able to code&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:33.840
or buy a bunch of software and figure out how&nbsp;
they work. This is going to change the world.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:40.620
We can also upload a file with a bunch&nbsp;
of data and ask GPT-4 to try to make some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:46.920
sense of it. And it does that beautifully.&nbsp;
This is low-key amazing: what it has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:53.160
given is just a bunch of numbers, and it had&nbsp;
to find out what part of this is interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:58.260
